.\" hydra-interactive(1)
.TH HYDRA\-INTERACTIVE 1 "2026-08-17" "hydra" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
hydra-interactive \- download manager with a persistent queue
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hydra interactive
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ URL ...]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a full-screen queue manager, or \(em with
.B \-\-headless
\(em works the same queue with no screen and one log line per event.
.PP
Any URLs on the command line are enqueued at startup.
The queue persists across sessions in a state file, so a later invocation
reattaches to it.
.PP
The subcommand declares its own options rather than borrowing the top-level
ones.
A subcommand competing with a variadic positional URL list is ambiguous in
both orders: with borrowed options
.B "hydra interactive \-\-queue\-file X"
rejects the flag, and
.B "hydra \-\-queue\-file X URL interactive"
swallows the word "interactive" as a URL.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-queue\-file " FILE"
Queue file.
Defaults to a per-user state directory \(em see
.BR FILES .
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Work the queue with no screen, one log line per event, checkpointing the
queue on start and every 2 seconds.
.TP
\fB\-n\fI N\fR, \fB\-\-max\-active\fI N\fR How many transfers run at once.
Default 2.
Adjustable live with
.B +
and
.BR \- ,
in the range 1-16.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Open the per-connection detail view for the selected item.
.TP
.B Esc
Leave the detail view.
Never quits.
.TP
.B a
Add a URL.
.B Backspace
edits while typing;
.B Esc
abandons the entry.
.TP
.BR j ", " k ", " Down ", " Up
Move the selection.
.TP
.BR p ", " r
Pause / resume the selected transfer.
.TP
.BR d ", " Delete
Cancel the selected transfer.
.TP
.BR J ", " K
Move the selected item down / up in the queue.
.TP
.B c
Clear finished and cancelled items.
.TP
.BR + ", " =
Raise queue parallelism by one.
.TP
.B \-
Lower queue parallelism by one.
.TP
.BR ? ", " h
Help overlay.
.TP
.B b
Background: leave the UI, transfers keep running.
.TP
.B q
Quit: stop the running transfers and exit.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Leave the UI immediately.
.
.SS Parallelism is not connection count
.B +
and
.B \-
set how many
.I queued items
may transfer simultaneously.
Each item still opens as many
.I connections
as the scheduler measures to be useful for its own mirrors, which is a
separate number chosen per path: on a link already saturated by one
connection, more connections add no speed, so the scheduler declines to open
them.
Raising this setting multiplies total connections; on a shared or metered
link it is the setting to lower first.
.
.SS Background and quit are different on purpose
.B b
detaches and leaves transfers running;
.B q
stops them.
Binding one key to both is how a large download gets lost by reflex, which
is also why
.B Esc
is never a quit key.
.PP
Backgrounding cannot mean merely leaving the event loop: the transfers are
tasks in the same process, so exiting would kill them and a reattaching
session would find everything stopped.
.B b
therefore re-executes the binary in headless queue mode inside a
.I new session
and streams its output to a log beside the queue file.
The headless worker checkpoints the queue on start and every 2 seconds, so a
reattaching UI sees live state along with the owning PID.
.PP
Queue items record their owner PID for that reason.
A reloaded queue demotes a
.B Running
item back to
.B Queued
only when that process is really gone \(em demoting a live one would put two
writers on one output file.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/hydra/queue.json
Default queue state.
Falls back to
.I $HOME/.local/state/hydra/queue.json
and then to
.I ./hydra/queue.json
when neither variable is set.
Override with
.BR \-\-queue\-file .
.TP
.I queue.log
Written beside the queue file (same path, extension replaced) by a
backgrounded headless worker.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for the default queue file.
.TP
.B HOME
Used when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the manager with two URLs queued:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
hydra interactive https://a.example/x.iso https://b.example/y.iso
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a queue on a server with no terminal, four at a time:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
hydra interactive \-\-headless \-n 4 \-\-queue\-file /srv/dl/queue.json
.fi
.RE
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hydra (1)
